# ============================================================================
# OraDiscuss - Audit and Governance Pack v1.0.0
# config.env - single configuration file sourced by audit_governance.sh.
#
# Published by OraDiscuss (oradiscuss.com). Not produced by, affiliated with,
# or endorsed by Oracle Corporation.
#
# Written for Oracle 19c/21c/23ai on Linux. Same config style as the other
# packs, so if you already run one of those you can copy your values across.
#
# SECURITY: this file must NEVER contain passwords. Scripts connect via
#           OS authentication ("sqlplus / as sysdba") by default.
# ============================================================================

# --- Oracle environment -----------------------------------------------------
# SID of the instance to read. There is no default, on purpose.
ORACLE_SID=""
ORACLE_HOME=""
# For a non-SYS reading account use a wallet TNS alias. Never a password here.
ORACLE_CONNECT="/ as sysdba"

# --- The window -------------------------------------------------------------
# How many days back the time-bounded tiers look: audit trail activity, the
# change inventory, and the audit trail hygiene read.
#
# THIS IS A BOUND, NOT A PREFERENCE. Without it those tiers would be a raw dump
# of the audit trail, which on a busy estate is millions of rows, is slow enough
# to be noticed by the people running the database, and produces a document
# nobody reads. Every tier that uses it states the window in its own text, so a
# reader of the report never has to come back to this file to know what period
# they are looking at.
AUDIT_WINDOW_DAYS=30

# --- How many rows a ranked tier lists --------------------------------------
# The privilege, grant, change and activity tiers rank their rows and keep the
# top N. A full listing of every grant in an estate is an export, not a report.
# The count that was kept is stated in the report beside the rows.
AUDIT_TOP_N=25

# --- Output -----------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT_DIR="$HOME/oradiscuss-audit/output"
